# Repo audit (Nov 2026) — clean-up before the 2026 deploy

Load assumed: ~10 family users, Docker + gunicorn.
Tests: 59 pass on Python 3.12; fail out of the box on 3.15 (pillow build).

## Must fix

1. [ ] Worker drift (`app.py` globals SS/ASSIGNMENTS/logins, Dockerfile `-w 4`).
   Redraw / set_password only update one of 4 workers; startup draw can race.
   Fix: `gunicorn -w 1 --threads 8`.
2. [ ] One-shot migrations run on every boot (`app.py` migrate_tredje_scores_to_fjerde,
   migrate_reindeer_rush_alias, remove_glaedelig_jul_game). Resetting fjerde-advent
   then restarting moves all tredje-advent scores into it. Fix: delete them.
3. [ ] No `.dockerignore`: `COPY .` ships `.env`, node_modules, scores.sqlite3 and
   test leftovers (tests write `secret-santa-<year>.json = {"jimmy": "camilla"}` into
   repo root, which would block the real draw). Fix: add `.dockerignore`, make tests
   use tmp_path (test_admin_games.py, test_navbar_and_pages.py, test_navbar_games_links.py).
4. [ ] `SECRET_KEY` falls back to `'dev-secret'` -> forgeable admin session.
   Fix: `os.environ['SECRET_KEY']`.
5. [ ] `CORS(app, supports_credentials=True)` reflects any origin. Same-origin app.
   Fix: remove CORS and flask-cors.
6. [ ] `POST /api/scores/<game>` needs no login, no name cap, any game key.
   Fix: login_required, `name[:20]`, known games only.

